{#
    The section bar: a hairline and a tracked-caps label, spanning the page
    frame. Used as a section heading on composed pages and as the page
    heading on the list-shaped index pages, which is why the heading level is
    a parameter rather than fixed — a page needs exactly one h1.

    The bar carries only its label. Facts about the list (a count, a date)
    go in the margin column; the way on from a list closes the list instead,
    with `listMore` below.
#}
{% macro sectionBar(label, level = 2) %}
<div class="section-bar">
    <h{{ level }} class="section-bar__label">{{ label }}</h{{ level }}>
</div>
{% endmacro %}

{#
    The way on from a list — "All essays", the full work history — set as the
    list's last line, in the main column.

    The arrow is drawn for on-site destinations only. An off-site one already
    carries the external-link icon the global rule hangs off every such
    anchor, and the two marks side by side say the same thing twice. The test
    is the one that rule makes — a "//" in the href — so a link cannot end up
    with both marks or with neither.
#}
{% macro listMore(label, href) %}
<p class="list-more"><a href="{{ href }}">{{ label }}{% if "//" not in href %}<span class="list-more__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>{% endif %}</a></p>
{% endmacro %}
